Step 1: Upload trained model to S3

Go to Amazon S3

Open AWS Console → search S3
Create bucket (if not created)
Upload your model file

Example:

model.tar.gz
model.pkl
model.joblib
model.pt
model.onnx

Typical path:

s3://my-bucket/model.tar.gz
Step 2: Create Model in SageMaker

Go to:

Amazon SageMaker → Deployments & inference → Deployable models

Click:

Create model

Fill fields:

Field	What to put
Model name	any name
IAM role	Create new role
Model data location	S3 path of model
Container	choose framework

Example containers:

Model type	Container
sklearn	Scikit-learn
pytorch	PyTorch
tensorflow	TensorFlow
custom	bring your own container

Click Create model

Step 3: Create Endpoint

Now go to:

Deployments & inference → Endpoints

Click:

Create endpoint

Fill:

Field	Value
Endpoint name	my-endpoint
Model	select model created above
Instance type	ml.t2.medium
Instance count	1

Click:

Create endpoint

Wait 5–10 minutes until:

Status = InService
Final result 🎯

You will get an API endpoint:

Endpoint name: my-endpoint
Service: SageMaker Runtime

Use in code:

runtime.invoke_endpoint(
 EndpointName="my-endpoint"
)
Easiest flow diagram
Faculty gives model
        ↓
Upload to S3
        ↓
Create model (SageMaker)
        ↓
Create endpoint
        ↓
API ready
Cheapest settings 💰

Use:

Instance type = ml.t2.medium
Instance count = 1

Then delete endpoint after demo to avoid cost.
